From 1910a8f719984b8aab0b405bbba419dc01b83a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 14:32:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: extract pure logic from class-based modules

Separate pure business logic from I/O-dependent class methods into
standalone *_logic.py modules. This enables:

1. Direct unit testing of pure functions without I/O side effects
2. Regression fingerprinting via output-based tools (e.g. Regrets)
3. Cleaner separation of concerns between logic and I/O shells

Changes:
- brainfuck_logic.py: preprocess(), compile_program(), eval_to_output()
  extracted from Brainfuck class
- brainloller_logic.py: to_brainfuck(), to_brainloller() extracted
  from Brainloller class
- braincopter_logic.py: decode_pixel(), find_similar(), to_brainfuck()
  extracted from Braincopter class
- brainfuck.py: delegates to brainfuck_logic, fixes 'is' -> '=='
  comparisons (eliminates Python 3.8+ SyntaxWarnings)
- brainloller.py: delegates to brainloller_logic
- braincopter.py: delegates to braincopter_logic

All existing tests pass. No behavioral changes.
Verified by Regrets output-based regression testing (7 clusters, 5-run
drift detection: all PASS+STABLE).
